To have an application which help in medication verification and patient accurate diagnosis
Categorization, Expiry Management and stock reconciliation and medication verification

Expiration checking :  Able to give easier access for expiration checking

Medication verification : To verify possible indication and contraindication and verification of identity of medicine

Having an access in MIMS



# 1. Core Objective of the Mobile Application

To **ensure patient safety, accurate medication verification, efficient expiry management, and reliable stock control**, using the client’s existing medication list and **verified drug information from MIMS**.

---

# 2. User Roles & Access Control

### 2.1 User Roles

- **Pharmacist**
- **Doctor / Clinician**
- **Inventory / Store Manager**
- **Administrator**

### 2.2 Role-Based Permissions

- Login with secure authentication (PIN / biometric)
- Access limited based on role
- Audit trail of user actions (who verified, adjusted stock, etc.)

---

# 3. Medication Master & Categorization

### 3.1 Medication Master (From Client List)

- Import client-provided medication list
- Brand name
- Generic name
- Strength
- Dosage form
- Manufacturer
- Therapeutic category
- Storage condition
- Controlled drug flag (if applicable)

### 3.2 Categorization Features

- By therapeutic class
- By dosage form
- By storage condition
- By expiry status
- By stock level

---

# 4. Medication Verification (Core Safety Feature)

### 4.1 Medication Identity Verification

- Barcode / QR code scanning
- Manual search
- Verify:
    - Brand & generic name
    - Strength & formulation
    - Manufacturer
    - Batch / lot number

### 4.2 Indication & Contraindication Check (MIMS)

- Approved indications
- Contraindications
- Drug–drug interactions
- Special warnings:
    - Pregnancy
    - Pediatric
    - Geriatric
    - Renal / hepatic impairment
- Clear “Source: MIMS” reference

---

# 5. Expiry Management

### 5.1 Expiry Data Capture

- Expiry date per batch
- Batch / lot tracking
- Manufacturing date (optional)

### 5.2 Expiry Monitoring

- Real-time expiry status
- Color-coded indicators:
    - Green – Safe
    - Yellow – Near expiry
    - Red – Expired

### 5.3 Expiry Alerts & Notifications

- Configurable alert periods (30/60/90 days)
- Push notifications
- Dashboard alerts

### 5.4 Quick Expiry Checking

- One-tap expiry check
- Scan medication → instant expiry status
- Filter expiring items by time range

---

# 6. Inventory & Stock Management

### 6.1 Stock Tracking

- Real-time stock quantity
- Batch-wise stock
- Storage location tracking

### 6.2 Stock Reconciliation

- Expected vs actual stock comparison
- Manual stock adjustment
- Reasons for adjustment:
    - Dispensed
    - Damaged
    - Expired
    - Lost

### 6.3 Stock Alerts

- Low stock alerts
- Out-of-stock alerts
- Overstock indicators

---

# 7. Patient Safety & Diagnosis Support (Supportive Only)

### 7.1 Patient Profile Entry

- Age
- Gender
- Weight (optional)
- Known allergies
- Existing conditions

### 7.2 Medication Suitability Check

- Match medication against patient profile
- Contraindication warnings
- Allergy alerts
- Duplicate therapy alerts

### 7.3 Clinical Disclaimer

- Clearly displayed:
    
    > “This application supports clinical decision-making and does not replace professional medical judgment.”
    > 

---

# 8. MIMS Integration

### 8.1 Drug Information Access

- Embedded MIMS drug monographs
- Search within medication details
- Structured sections:
    - Indications
    - Contraindications
    - Dosage
    - Warnings
    - Interactions

### 8.2 Offline & Performance

- Cache frequently used drug data
- Read-only offline access (if licensed)

---

# 9. Dashboard & User Interface

### 9.1 Home Dashboard

- Expiry alerts
- Low stock alerts
- Quick statistics:
    - Total medications
    - Near-expiry count
    - Expired items

### 9.2 Visual Indicators

- Icons & color codes
- Minimal text, expandable sections
- Fast navigation

---

# 10. Search & Filtering

- Search by:
    - Brand name
    - Generic name
    - Category
- Filters:
    - Expiry date
    - Stock level
    - Therapeutic class
    - Dosage form

---

# 11. Reports & Analytics

### 11.1 Standard Reports

- Expiry report
- Stock movement report
- Reconciliation report
- Medication verification history

### 11.2 Export Options

- PDF / Excel export
- Date-range selection

---

# 12. Notifications & Alerts

- Expiry alerts
- Low stock alerts
- System alerts
- Role-specific notifications

